{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The capacitor assortment fits my circuit experiments because it complements the breadboards, PCB supplies, and electronic components I have used.",
    "The small M2 and M3 hardware assortment feels useful for mounting circuit boards and assembling electronics projects, subject to checking the sizes I need."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The acrylic sheet, sanding wheels, taps, and steel rods require particular fabrication tasks that I have no current reason to undertake.",
    "The syringe and duct reducer serve jobs absent from my history, while the large sheet-metal screws do not match the small electronics mounting tasks I have in mind.",
    "Having used adhesive fasteners does not mean I currently need adhesive magnets; the mounting purpose matters more than the shared adhesive backing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been taken as broad interest in almost any DIY tool or workshop material.",
    "Occasional purchases such as casters and fasteners seem to suggest more ongoing mechanical work than my history supports."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, PCB supplies, relay module, and battery holder form a connected pattern of circuit building that makes compatible components especially relevant.",
    "I choose specialized supplies when they fit a concrete task; dimensions, electrical specifications, and compatibility matter more than a general association with DIY."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my electronics projects but stretch that interest into unrelated workshop tasks without a clear current need."
}"}
